# Rydia's Return ({3}{G}{G}, sorcery), "Return up to two target permanent cards from your graveyard to your hand." On turn 1 Bot1
# puts a Black Lotus, an Ornithopter, a Llanowar Elves and two Lightning Bolts into its graveyard (the Lotus pays for the two Bolts
# that kill its own creatures), and Bot2 puts its own Black Lotus into its graveyard on turn 2. On turn 9 (Emerald and four Forests:
# exactly the five mana the spell costs) a Bolt (not a permanent card), Bot2's Lotus (the wrong graveyard) and three permanent
# cards (more than "up to two") are refused; Bot1 takes the Ornithopter and the Lotus. The Elves and the Bolts stay behind, and
# Bot2's graveyard (three discarded Islands and the Lotus) is untouched.

